ris (January 5, 2022). [\\\"These Are the People Who Died in Connection With the Capitol Riot\\\"](https://www.nytimes.com/2022/01/05/us/politics/jan-6-capitol-deaths.html). _[The New York Times](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_New_York_Times \\\"The New York Times\\\")_. Retrieved January 29, 2022.\\n  424. **[^](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donald_Trump#cite_ref-FOOTNOTEPion-BerlinBruneauGoetze2022_430-0)** [Pion-Berlin, Bruneau & Goetze 2022](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donald_Trump#CITEREFPion-BerlinBruneauGoetze2022).\\n  425. **[^](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donald_Trump#cite_ref-FOOTNOTEHarvey20223\\\"Unlike_Hitler's_coup_attempt,_Trump_already_held_the_top_of_the_office,_so_he_was_attempting_to_hold_onto_power,_not_seize_it_\\\\(the_precise_term_for_Trump's_intended_action_is_a_'self-coup'_or_'autogolpe'\\\\)._Thus,_Trump_was_able_to_plan_for_the_event_well_in_advance_and_with_much_greater_control,_including_developing_the_legal_arguments_that_could_be_used_to_justify_rejecting_the_election's_results\\\"_431-0)** [Harvey 2022](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donald_Trump#CITEREFHarvey2022), p. 3, \\\"Unlike Hitler's coup attempt, Trump already held the top of the office, so he was attempting to hold onto power, not seize it (the precise term for Trump's intended action is a 'self-coup' or 'autogolpe'). Thus, Trump was able to plan for the event well in advance and with much greater control, including developing the legal arguments that could be used to justify rejecting the election's results\\\".\\n  426. **[^](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donald_Trump#cite_ref-FOOTNOTECasta%C3%B1edaJenks2023246\\\"What_the_United_States_went_through_on_January_6th_was_an_attempt_at_a_self-coup,_where_Trump_would_use_force_to_stay_as_head_of_state_even_if_abandoning_democratic_practices_in_the_U.S._Some_advised_Trump_to_declare_martial_law_to_create_a_state_of_emergency_and_use_that_as_an_excuse_to_stay_in_power\\\"_432-0)** [Castañeda & Jenks 2023](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donald_Trump#CITEREFCasta%C3%B1edaJenks2023), p. 246, \\\"What the United States went through on January 6th was an attempt at a self-coup, where Trump would use force to stay as head of state even if abandoning democratic practices in the U.S. Some advised Trump to declare martial law to create a state of emergency and use that as an excuse to stay in power\\\".\\n  427. **[^](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donald_Trump#cite_ref-434)** Wolfe, Jan (January 27, 2021). [\\\"Explainer: Why Trump's post-presidency perks, like a pension and office, are safe for the rest of his life\\\"](https://www.reuters.com/article/us-usa-trump-impeachment-benefits-explai-idUSKBN29W238). _[Reuters](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reuters \\\"Reuters\\\")_. Retrieved February 2, 2021.\\n  428. **[^](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donald_Trump#cite_ref-435)** Solender, Andrew (May 3, 2021). [\\\"Trump Says He'll Appropriate 'The Big Lie' To Refer To His Election Loss\\\"](https://www.forbes.com/sites/andrewsolender/2021/05/03/trump-says-hell-appropriate-the-big-lie-to-refer-to-his-election-loss/). _[Forbes](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forbes \\\"Forbes\\\")_. Retrieved October 10, 2021.\\n  429. **[^](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donald_Trump#cite_ref-key2_436-0)** Wolf, Zachary B. (May 19, 2021). [\\\"The 5 key elements of Trump's Big Lie and how it came to be\\\"](https://cnn.com/2021/05/19/politics/donald-trump-big-lie-explainer/). _[CNN](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CNN \\\"CNN\\\")_. Retrieved October 10, 2021.\\n  430. **[^](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donald_Trump#cite_ref-437)** [Balz, Dan](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dan_Balz \\\"Dan Balz\\\") (May 29, 2021). [\\\"The GOP push to revisit 2020 has worrisome implications for future elections\\\"](https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/trump-big-lie-elections-impact/2021/05/29/d7992fa2-c07d-11eb-b26e-53663e6be6ff_story.html). _[The Washington Post](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Washington_Post \\\"The Washing