ants charged in the Jan. 6 Capitol attack\\\"](https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/justice-department/trump-set-pardon-defendants-stormed-capitol-jan-6-2021-rcna187735). _[NBC News](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NBC_News \\\"NBC News\\\")_. Retrieved January 23, 2025.\\n  553. **[^](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donald_Trump#cite_ref-NPR2025_561-0)** [\\\"The Jan. 6 attack: The cases behind the biggest criminal investigation in U.S. history\\\"](https://www.npr.org/2021/02/09/965472049/the-capitol-siege-the-arrested-and-their-stories). _[NPR News](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NPR_News \\\"NPR News\\\")_. March 14, 2025. Retrieved April 14, 2025.\\n  554. **[^](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donald_Trump#cite_ref-562)** [Horsley, Scott](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scott_Horsley \\\"Scott Horsley\\\"); [Simon, Scott](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scott_Simon \\\"Scott Simon\\\") (January 25, 2025). [\\\"Trump inherits a strong economy by the numbers. What's his plan to lower prices?\\\"](https://www.npr.org/2025/01/25/nx-s1-5270829/trump-inherits-a-strong-economy-by-the-numbers-whats-his-plan-to-lower-prices). _[NPR News](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NPR_News \\\"NPR News\\\")_. \\\"[Mark Zandi](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mark_Zandi \\\"Mark Zandi\\\"): The numbers speak for themselves. Growth is strong. Lots of jobs. Unemployment is low. If you take the economy on the whole, it really is about as good as it gets. So President Trump is inheriting a fantastic economy.\\\"\\n  555. **[^](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donald_Trump#cite_ref-563)** Rugaber, Christopher (January 23, 2025). [\\\"Trump's inheriting a solid economy, making it harder to lower borrowing costs or inflation\\\"](https://apnews.com/article/trump-economy-inflation-interest-rates-borrowing-6ef86392b080ca963ec633546009409b). _[AP News](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AP_News \\\"AP News\\\")_. Retrieved January 23, 2025.\\n  556. **[^](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donald_Trump#cite_ref-564)** Ryssdal, Kai; Terenzio, Sofia (November 6, 2024). [\\\"Trump inherits a sturdy economy\\\"](https://www.marketplace.org/2024/11/06/strong-economy-next-president-inflation-employment/). _[Marketplace](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marketplace_\\\\(radio_program\\\\) \\\"Marketplace \\\\(radio program\\\\)\\\")_. Retrieved January 23, 2025.\\n  557. **[^](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donald_Trump#cite_ref-565)** [Casselman, Ben](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ben_Casselman \\\"Ben Casselman\\\") (December 18, 2024). [\\\"The Economy Is Finally Stable. Is That About to Change?\\\"](https://www.nytimes.com/2024/12/18/business/economy/trump-us-economy.html). _[The New York Times](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_New_York_Times \\\"The New York Times\\\")_. Retrieved January 23, 2025.\\n  558. **[^](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donald_Trump#cite_ref-566)** Smart, Tim (January 9, 2025). [\\\"Trump Will Inherit a Better Economy Than He Left Behind\\\"](https://www.usnews.com/news/u-s-news-decision-points/articles/2025-01-09/trump-to-inherit-a-better-economy-than-he-left-behind). _[U.S. News& World Report](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/U.S._News_%26_World_Report \\\"U.S. News & World Report\\\")_. Retrieved January 23, 2025.\\n  559. **[^](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donald_Trump#cite_ref-567)** Baker, Peter (January 5, 2025). [\\\"Trump Sees the U.S. as a 'Disaster.' The Numbers Tell a Different Story\\\"](https://www.nytimes.com/2025/01/05/us/politics/trump-us-disaster-numbers.html). _[The New York Times](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_New_York_Times \\\"The New York Times\\\")_. Retrieved January 23, 2025.\\n  560. **[^](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donald_Trump#cite_ref-569)** Plumer, Brad; Friedman, Lisa (April 11, 2025). [\\\"Trump's New Way to Kill Regulations: Because I Say So\\\"](https://www.nytimes.com/2025/04/11/climate/trump-regulations.html). _[The New York Times](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_New_York_Times \\\"The New York Times\\\")_. Retrieved August 23, 2025. \\\"In another order, he directed a rollback of federal rules that limit the water flow in shower heads with a highly unusual legal justification: Because I say so. \\\"Notice and comment is unnecessary because I am ordering the repeal,\\\" Mr. Trump's order said. Legal experts called that sentence astonishing and contrary to decades of federal law.\\\"\\n  561. **[^](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donald_Trump#cite_ref-570)** Joselow, Maxine; Natanson, Hannah; Duncan, Ian (May 18, 2025). [\\\"Trump orders the government to stop enforcing rules he doesn't like\\\"](https://www.washingtonpost.com/nation/2025/05/18/trump-enforcement-halt-regulations-laws/). _[The Washington Post](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Washington_Post \\\"The Washington Post\\\")_. Retrieved August 23, 2025.\\n  562. **[^](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donald_Trump#cite_ref-571)** Aspan, Maria (August 14, 2025). [\\\"Trump is tightening the screws on corporate America — and CEOs are staying mum\\\"](https://www.npr.org/2025/08/14/nx-s1-5501591/trump-corporate-america-capitalism). _[NPR News](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NPR_News \\\"NPR News\\\")_. Retrieved August 24, 2025. \\\"By demanding a cut of a private company's sales, in exchange for the right to do business, Trump is defying the traditionally Republican gospel of free-market capitalism.\\\"\\n  563. **[^](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donald_Trump#cite_ref-Morrow_08202025_572-0)** Morrow, Allison; Mattingly, Phil (August 20, 2025). [\\\"Corporate America is silent as Trump abandons free-market principles\\\"](https://www.cnn.com/2025/08/20/business/companies-trump-free-market). _[CNN](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CNN \\\"CNN\\\")_. Retrieved August 24, 2025.\\n  564. **[^](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donald_Trump#cite_ref-Wiles_08222025_573-0)** Wile, Rob (August 22, 2025). [\\\"U.S. takes 10% stake in Intel as Trump flexes more power over big business\\\"](https://www.nbcnews.com/business/business-news/intel-agrees-us-stake-in-company-how-much-what-to-know-rcna226667). _[NBC News](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NBC_News \\\"NBC News\\\")_. Retrieved August 24, 2025. \\\"Trump continues to bulldoze through long-held norms regarding government and business, departing from the free-market ethos that has long prevailed in both major U.S. political parties.\\\"\\n  565. **[^](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donald_Trump#cite_ref-574)** Sutton, Sam; Guida, Victoria (August 22, 2025). [\\\"Trump is turning the government into an investment firm\\\"](https://www.politico.com/newsletters/morning-money-capital-risk/2025/08/22/trump-is-turning-the-government-into-an-investment-firm-00519364). _[Politico](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Politico \\\"Politico\\\")_. Retrieved August 24, 2025. \\\"From tariff carveouts to pro bono legal work from white-shoe law firms, Trump is exerting power over U.S. businesses in ways that go beyond even Sen. Bernie Sanders's (I-Vt.) aspirations. His ability to inject his agenda into private enterprises and dealmaking has shaken the guardrails that protect businesses from sudden political shifts and defied the free-market orthodoxy that was a hallmark of Republican economic policymaking.\\\"\\n  566. **[^](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donald_Trump#cite_ref-575)** Johnson, Keith; Lu, Christina (July 16, 2025). [\\\"Trump Embraces State Capitalism\\\"](https://foreignpolicy.com/2025/07/16/trump-economy-industry-state-capitalism-steel-rare-earth-investment/). _[Foreign Policy](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Foreign_Policy \\\"Foreign Policy\\\")_. Retrieved August 24, 2025.\\n  567. **[^](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donald_Trump#cite_ref-Economist_08132025_576-0)** [\\\"Trump wants to command bosses like Xi does. He is failing\\\"](https://www.economist.com/business/2025/08/13/trump-wants-to-command-bosses-like-xi-does-he-is-failing). _[The Economist](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Economist \\\"The Economist\\\")_. August 13, 2025. Retrieved August 24, 2025. \\\"Thankfully, Mr Trump only dabbles in state capitalism. Even so, his approach is damaging.\\\"\\n  568. **[^](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donald_Trump#cite_ref-577)** Morrow, Allison (August 13, 2025). [\\\"Trump is tightening his grip on the economy, taking a page from China\\\"](https://www.cnn.com/2025/08/13/business/trump-economy-capitalism-nightcap). _[CNN](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CNN \\\"CNN\\\")_. Retrieved August 24, 2025. \\\"Trump's realignment of American business also bears similarities to China's model of \\\"state capitalism\\\" — a mix between socialism and classic free-market capitalism in which the state is involved in, but doesn't directly own, private businesses.\\\"\\n  569. **[^](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donald_Trump#cite_ref-578)** [Casselman, Ben](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ben_Casselman \\\"Ben Casselman\\\") (March 31, 2025). [\\\"Trump's Science Policies Pose Long-Term Risk, Economists Warn\\\"](https://www.nytimes.com/2025/03/31/business/economy/trump-research-cutbacks-economy.html). _[The New York Times](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_New_York_Times \\\"The New York Times\\\")_. Retrieved April 3, 2025.\\n  570. **[^](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donald_Trump#cite_ref-579)** Waldman, Annie (June 17, 2025). [\\\"Federal Judge Deems Trump Administration's Termination of NIH Grants Illegal\\\"](https://www.propublica.org/article/trump-nih-grant-terminations-illegal). _[ProPublica](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ProPublica \\\"ProPublica\\\")_. Retrieved August 16, 2025.\\n  571. **[^](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donald_Trump#cite_ref-580)** Fischler, Jacob (August 7, 2025). [\\\"Trump illegally froze 1,800 NIH medical research grants, Congress' watchdog says\\\"](https://www.govexec.com/oversight/2025/08/trump-illegally-froze-1800-nih-medical-research-grants-congress-watchdog-says/407296/?oref=ge-homepage-river). _[Government Executive](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Government_Executive \\\"Government Executive\\\")_